------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications by sam-mt
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The sam-mt modifications add transparent DFS (Distributed File
System) referral following to the SMB2 client. These are licensed under
the same 2-clause BSD license as the upstream work (see LICENSE).

The modifications consist of, principally:

  * internal/dfsc/      - MS-DFSC referral request/response codec
  * dfs.go              - DFS referral IOCTL transport (IPC$ / FSCTL)
  * dfs_resolver.go     - DFS referral resolution loop
  * dfs_cache.go        - DFS referral cache (TTL, longest-prefix)
  * dfs_conn.go         - backing-server connection map
  * client.go,          - Dialer.EnableDFS opt-in, Mount/op DFS hooks,
    client_fs.go,         persisted Dialer/Initiator for backing dials
    tree_conn.go,
    session.go

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Microsoft Open Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The DFS referral codec (internal/dfsc) implements the wire format
defined in the publicly published Microsoft Open Specifications document
[MS-DFSC]: Distributed File System (DFS): Referral Protocol
(https://learn.microsoft.com/openspecs/windows_protocols/ms-dfsc/).

Implementation of these published specifications is covered by the
Microsoft Open Specification Promise. No copyrighted source code from
any third-party DFS implementation was used in writing the
internal/dfsc package.
